# M2's keyboard focus ring on the page. Tab from no focus goes to the first stop, the wordmark
# (its ring at radius 6), then the gear (its line --primary under the ring), then the function
# picker's picked option (x², 148.25 to 245.5 at 1440 x 900), then a's flip toggle and a's number
# box (330, 408.5, 107, 32), with the keys' tip under a's row: a 3 px ring outside each in primary
# at 32 %, its corners the part's own spread. A press on row k's name clears the ring, as
# :focus-visible does. These are Chromium's stops (plan call 3 f): WebKit's Tab skips the link and
# the buttons (AGENTS.md), its fifth landing on h's box, so the shots are judged against Chromium.
# The page waits 2 s first, as M6's states do, so React's plane has finished its first paint.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
tab
wait 16
shot wordmark
tab
wait 16
shot gear
tab
wait 16
shot picker
tab
tab
wait 16
shot box
click 200 468
wait 16
shot pressed
